# 2026-08-28 10:50:59.547934
+As you may have noticed, I have created thr current working folder as a subfolder in my Openclaw workspace. I have been using Openclaw to help me build this project. What I like to call the due-dilligence project is actually a sub project of the bigger AIdriven.biz project. AIdriven.biz is my business name as well as my web address. You can read more about the overall The overall mission is to provide AI services to SMME companies in New Zealand.You can read more about the history so far in the file memory.md in the root of the workspace. This file is the main memory of my Openclaw agent  called Sebastian, or Seb for short). The website loca files is in the \aidriven-website directory. The file aidriven-website\index-new.html is the root of the website which is hosted on Cloudflare pages. In the aidriven-website\property\index.html is the Beta test site that we are working on at the moment. We have run into some blockers at the moment with the LINZ integration. The basic workflow is that the customer completes a google form on the web page. On submission a google sheet is updated with the field values submitted. The form has an attached Onsubmit function which passes the information to a Cloudflare worker via API interface. The worker then sends the client an confirmation email and stores the data in a KV namespace. From there an Openclaw cron job olls the KV workspace and as soon as it sees a new request, it creates the report. The report generation script creates the report locally in html format in the local reports\html folder. From there it is pushed to Github pages from where it is served to the customer. The report generator then generates an email that is sent to the customer with the link for their report. The whole workflow is automated using the Openclaw agent as orchestrator. However, we have run into a number of obstacles. The most pressing is the interface into LINZ data services API to draw data from various layers and to display relevant maps on the report (mostly regarding Hazards). All current scripts in the repository can be used as examples and guides but should not be changed unless I give permission. I want to basically re-start the project in the current working directory independently of what has already been done. I do still want to use Openclaw agent as the overall process coordinator, but I am happy to redevelop any/or all functionality in whatever language is most suitable for the requirement. I am not a techie, but most of the examples that I have sen of the functionality that is required is written in python. I'd be happy if python forms the backbone of the development.

